//! task: write
//! ask: Return the 16-bit CCITT initial value 0xffff and the polynomial 0x1021 as constants.
//! expect: ok
//! refs: §8.4
//! explain: An integer literal is a run of decimal digits or `0x` plus hexadecimal digits, either case. The value is typed by what it lands in, so a literal too wide for its type is EXS-E0308. There are no binary or octal literals and no digit separators `[OPEN]`.

publica functio initialis() -> u16 {
    redde 0xffff;
}

publica functio polynomium() -> u16 {
    redde 0x1021;
}
